cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Option-Implied Bubble Detection
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the underlying paper and, if you
  used this implementation specifically, this repository.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Adzic
    given-names: Luka
    affiliation: University of Pennsylvania
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/lukaadzic/option-implied-bubbles
url: https://financial-bubble.vercel.app
abstract: >-
  An interactive dashboard and reference estimator for option-implied financial
  bubble detection, covering the S&P 500 and 26 US equities from 1996 to 2023.
  Fundamental value is recovered from the cross-section of option prices rather
  than assumed from a pricing model, following Jarrow and Kwok (2021). Includes
  a Python implementation of the estimator's core identity and a synthetic-data
  harness that verifies unbiased recovery and honest confidence-interval
  coverage.
keywords:
  - asset pricing
  - financial bubbles
  - option pricing
  - put-call parity
  - risk-neutral valuation
  - econometrics
  - data visualization
license: Apache-2.0
